Title: Color fig_census_direct points by model family (EN/FR/ZH)
Created: 2026-05-21
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-21T08:00Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Figure 1 in the manuscript (`fig_census_direct.pdf`, generated by
`src/aedist/plot_method_convergence.py`) currently colors each model
with a hash-derived hue (`_model_color`). The manuscript's Annex A
explicitly groups the 16 journal-lineup models by language family
(EN: Anthropic + OpenAI, FR: Mistral, ZH: Alibaba + DeepSeek). A
family-coded palette would let readers see family-level patterns at a
glance (e.g. whether EN frontier consistently beats ZH mid-tier) without
cross-referencing the table.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_method_convergence.py` — `_model_color()` at line ~28
  derives a per-model hue from the model slug. Replace with a family-aware
  palette.
- `experiments/experiments.toml` — `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]` is
  the source of truth for family assignment, but the per-model `family`
  attribute lives in the model registry.
- `src/aedist/models.py` (or wherever model metadata is defined) — check
  whether `family` is already a registered field.

## Actions

1. Confirm where model family is recorded (model registry vs. inferred
   from lab/slug). If not already a field, add `family: "EN" | "FR" | "ZH"`
   to the registered models in the journal lineup.
2. Replace `_model_color()` with a family-aware palette: pick three
   colorblind-safe hues (e.g. ColorBrewer Set2 or Wong) and map each model
   to its family hue. Optionally vary lightness within family to keep
   adjacent models distinguishable.
3. Add a small in-figure legend (or update the annotation overlay in
   `slides/slides.tex` if cleaner) showing the family-color mapping.
4. Rebuild `slides/inputs/generated/fig_census_direct.pdf` and
   `report/inputs/generated/fig_census_direct.pdf` via the existing
   Makefile targets.

## Test

- Add a unit test in `tests/test_plot_method_convergence.py` (create if
  absent): assert that `_family_color("claude-opus-4.6") == _family_color("gpt-5.5")`
  (both EN) and differs from `_family_color("mistral-large-2512")` (FR)
  and `_family_color("deepseek-v4-pro")` (ZH).

## Invariants

- The figure layout (bar arrangement, dashed-green reference line, model
  ordering) must not change — only the bar colors do.
- The report-side figure (which uses the broader `census` prompt-version
  with ~37 models, not all in the journal lineup) must still render
  cleanly. Define a fallback color for models without a family attribute.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each model bar in `fig_census_direct.pdf` is colored by family
- [ ] Legend or annotation makes the EN/FR/ZH mapping explicit
- [ ] Unit test covers the family-color mapping
- [ ] `make slides/slides.pdf` and `make report/inputs/generated/fig_census_direct.pdf` both build cleanly
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
